    fix(namespaces): extend in-flight-push guard to REST and MCP deletion paths (DF-0923-01)
    
    deleteNamespace() - the shared core behind DELETE /api/namespaces/:name and
    MCP delete_namespace - now refuses while an S3 push is in flight, inheriting
    the guard the CLI (deleteNamespaceFromDisk) always had. Live-proven gap:
    with a valid sync lock held, CLI delete-disk errored "Push in flight" while
    REST DELETE returned 200 and the dir was gone (dogfood 2026-09-23).
    
    - extract hasInFlightPush into leaf module src/namespaces/inflight-push.ts
      (delete.ts cannot import from lifecycle.ts - lifecycle imports delete);
      lifecycle.ts re-exports for existing importers, zero CLI behavior change
    - guard in the core after path-safety, before rmSync/manifest unlink,
      reusing the GAP-062 config-resolved namespaces root
    - REST route maps "Push in flight" refusals to 409 CONFLICT
    - new suite delete-inflight-df0923-01.test.ts (5 tests): BLOCKED (dir +
      mapping intact), stale-lock proceeds, dead-pid proceeds, REST 409,
      guards sanity; RED-verified 2/5 failing pre-fix (foreman control run)
    - AGENTS.md count sync: 165/1325 -> 166/1330
    
    Gates: vitest 1330/1330 (166 files), tsc --noEmit clean, prettier --check src/ clean.
    Also carries gitreins record for gap062 (completed 2026-09-22T22:29Z, uncommitted).
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
